  "term": "Cornell Medical Index",
  "definition": "The Cornell Medical Index is a self-completed health questionnaire used to gather medical history information to support a medical interview. Its questions cover both physical symptoms and patterns of mood and feelings, and it has also been used in personality assessment and epidemiologic research.",
